This learning experience meets three learning objectives:

  1. Demonstrate to the students the value of “scanning,” that is, picking out a few relevant details from a document, rather than trying to read it word for word;
  2. Introduce students to the idea that scanning is not just a parochial practice; it was employed by philologists in the nineteenth and early twentieth century;
